ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the A7 RegenEfficiency / LifetimeStats / Geofences precedents)
  TemperatureImpactPageModel.kt      framework-free: registration ids; parseTemperatureImpact
                                     (decodes GET /analytics/temperature-impact → List<TempEfficiencyPoint>,
                                     web `res.points ?? []`); TEMP_BUCKETS_C + tempBucketIndex + bucketLabel
                                     (web getTempBucketIndex / bucketLabel); TemperatureDisplayPrefs (web useUnits)
                                     — convertTempFromSI + the inline KM_PER_MILE Wh/km→Wh/mi factor at the
                                     boundary (web notes there is no convertEfficiencyFromSI helper);
                                     deriveTemperatureStats (web stats useMemo: avgEff, bucketAvgs, best/worst,
                                     total); scatterPoints (web scatterData); computeScatterLayout (pure scatter
                                     geometry + the avg ReferenceLine fraction); temperatureTips (web tips useMemo);
                                     recordTemperatureImpactPageOpened (view.opened); mapData.
  TemperatureImpactPageIcons.kt      locally-authored stroked 24×24 glyphs (Thermometer, Sun, Lightbulb,
                                     TrendingUp, Activity); Snowflake re-exported from DataDisplayGlyphs (the
                                     LifetimeStatsPageIcons precedent — shared catalogs unedited, out of scope).
  TemperatureImpactPageSource.kt     seam over container.api (GET /analytics/temperature-impact?vehicle_id via
                                     the shared resilient safeRequest, folded to a loading→success/error Resource
                                     stream — the GeofencesPageSource api.request precedent, since the web issues
                                     this read inline through request() and AnalyticsRepository carries no
                                     temperature-impact port) + SelectedVehicleStore (web useSelectedVehicle) +
                                     SettingsStore.settings (web useUnits). No HTTP in the view.
  TemperatureImpactPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; pointsState: StateFlow<UiState<List<TempEfficiencyPoint>>>
                                     re-collected on vehicle/refresh, empty when the list is empty or no vehicle is
                                     selected (web `enabled: vehicleId !== ''` / `!points?.length`); displayPrefs
                                     StateFlow (web useUnits); refresh/retry/recordViewOpened. No HTTP in the view.
  TemperatureImpactPage.kt           stateless TemperatureImpactPageContent + the eight Material 3 panels; the
                                     points feed is folded by the framework-free model into the cards, the native
                                     Canvas scatter (with its avg reference line), the A3 line wrapper, the optimal
                                     analysis, and the tips. SI→display only at the boundary via prefs.
  TemperatureImpactPageHost.kt       registers TemperatureImpactRoute for the `temperatureImpact` destination
                                     (Destinations.kt L102, /temperature-impact); wired in
                                     TeslaSyncApplication.onCreate() (NavHost registration).

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  The points stay SI on the wire (°C, Wh/km). Display conversion happens only at the render boundary via
  TemperatureDisplayPrefs.toTemperatureDisplay (shared convertTempFromSI) and toDisplayEff (the inline KM_PER_MILE
  Wh/km→Wh/mi factor — there is no convertEfficiencyFromSI helper, exactly as the web page documents). The SI source
  is never stored converted (Phase-48 SI-canonical; ADR-013 keeps the cache SI).

LIVE DATA / STALENESS (ADR-013)
  The single source is the inline `/analytics/temperature-impact` read (not an SSE live feed), surfaced as a
  loading→success/error Resource stream projected to UiState, so there is no >2 min live-staleness badge (no live
  source on this page — the web page likewise renders no freshness chip).

